{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483477-why-do-most-of-the-cod-posts-seem-to-be-about-rules-instead-of-setting-lore","id":1483477,"title":"Why do most of the CoD posts seem to be about rules instead of setting lore?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-09T10:07:33-07:00","id":1483477,"title":"Why do most of the CoD posts seem to be about rules instead of setting lore?","content":"Is it because the CoD doesn\u2019t have much setting lore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T10:31:31-07:00","id":1483480,"title":"","content":"It does, if you use the God Machine stuff, which I have personally shied away from. <br /> <br /> I think the biggest strength (and possibly weakness) of Chronicles of Darkness is that it was very bare-bones in design. There's no Metaplot, outside what your storyteller chooses.<br /> <br /> Another thing is when the first edition was out, it was seen mostly as a jumping-off point into Vampire, Werewolf, et al. Back then, you needed the core CoD book for a lot of basic stuff to make your character (which I found at least inconvenient and one player found VERY inconvenient). The idea was you'd make a human with the CoD book, have a Chronicle, and THEN you became a monster. 2nd Edition did away with that but I think a lot of damage was already done, and good will burnt by then. <br /> <br /> Ultimately though, in Chronicles of Darkness, you make your own lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T10:33:12-07:00","id":1483482,"title":"","content":"CofD has plenty of setting lore. What it has less of is a) metaplot developments where actions occur and the setting changes over time (these exist but are rare, such as Vampire's material on New Orleans reflecting the effects of Hurricane Katrina) and b) major NPCs whose backgrounds snake their way through many different books in ways that change the understanding of who they are, like arguing about the background of Ur-Shulgi or plots by Mithras.<br /> <br /> One major reason is that CofD books, for the most part, try to avoid content that requires you to be buying multiple supplement books to understand and use it. A signature character might be mentioned in multiple supplements, but if the Sakadagami, the Thai covenant of Buddhist vampires, is introduced in Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines, you won't see another supplement dedicate a big passage to a plot hook that depends upon introducing characters who've studied the covenant's attainments and are reviving their feud against the forces of wildness traditionally symbolized by the Bird, or if it does it will have to spend wordcount on reintroducing the Sakadagami and its stuff for people who haven't read those other books. Connections born of setting elements introduced in supplements thus tend more often to be sidelong allusions of the sort readers don't really need to know full detail to use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T11:08:17-07:00","id":1483492,"title":"","content":"Echoing Stupid Loserman:<br /> <br /> There's a lot of setting in the CofD. However it is, by design, never &quot;correct.&quot; So... there's not a lot to discuss/argue/debate/etc. The answer is always, &quot;how you want it to be in your game.&quot; So all the lore has to fit into the design mold of, &quot;how is this useful to as many tables as possible, or at least people that would use the book this is in&quot; rather than, &quot;is this cool for world building?&quot; <br /> <br /> As such, there's far less discussion about it because... discussing it here doesn't really help people as much as it does in games (like the WoD) where you'll know more about your private games by talking to people online about the setting in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T11:24:12-07:00","id":1483496,"title":"","content":"I do like that Chronicles gives you a <i>lot</i> of room to customize the setting to your liking. They give good guidelines for building things, and then allow you to run wild.<br /> <br /> I've certainly done my share of customization when brainstorming settings, such as cold iron not being a universal weakness of True Fae when said True Fae is based on something in folklore that isn't affected by cold iron (e.g. youkai), being possible to bring Rippers back from the brink even after an initial kill, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T14:15:32-07:00","id":1483514,"title":"","content":"Simply put, because in CoD the lore is what <b>you</b> as ST wants it to be first and foremost, with the added spin of ideas and concepts brought by your own players.<br /> <br /> The books matter as little or as much as you want them to and you can break, remake and mix up bits &amp; pieces however you feels like.<br /> <br /> Once a bunch of years ago, i made a topic joking about how Project Valkyrie - from Hunter: the Vigil, in case you're unfamiliar - can be crazily obsessive with the norse name-theming of their high-tech gear for an american secret agency....<br /> <br /> <br /> Half a dozen posts and other people comments later, it had somehow mutated in &quot;the Collection of Heroes&quot;, a HtV/Immortals/Scion chronicle about how the Project was in truth a front for the <b>literal</b> valkyries, sending soldiers to fight the monsters, so those who died but proved themselves would be gathered for Valhalla as Einherjar for the time when Ragnarok approached.<br /> <br /> <br /> My last Requiem chronicle had 3-4 different types of vampire progenitors beside the Strix with interests &amp; vices of their own, 3 spirit realms connected with the kindred but with strange inhabitants of their own that could be ally, enemy or both, not to mention all kinds of convoluted supernatural conflict and intrigue related to these beings and more, all glued together through a mess of brazilian folklore mixed with bits and pieces stolen from Forsaken and Awakening (though i never used any Uratha or Awakened in my games).<br /> <br /> My bad, i did use a group of Uratha, once. They were a cult dedicated to St Christopher and closer to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> than anything like the core tribes or lodges.<br /> <br /> The shapechanger clans i actually used with some regularity were even more homebrewed and weirder, believe me.<br /> <br /> <br /> You make so much of your own, so there's much less reason to debate official setting lore - because simply put, not even being book lore makes it canon, if you do <b>not </b>want it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-09-2022, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T14:49:31-07:00","id":1483520,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T14:50:14-07:00","id":1483521,"title":"","content":"A minor quibble because I find it frustrating how the word gets tossed around: the book lore is canon because that's what canon means. The CofD is just designed such that you can toss the canon book lore all you want and the games don't break if you do (there are multiple books that even talk about how to do it). The WoD games, on the other hand, lean far more into their canon setting such that there are a lot of load-bearing setting elements that if you remove things fall apart.<br /> <br /> Canon is only useful as a concept regarding what an accepted authority says is and isn't canon. In this case, canon is useful for things like, &quot;third party material from the STV isn't canon,&quot; so that if you do choose to use it in your games, and it doesn't work right, that's not on Onyx Path. Or &quot;the TT RPG books &gt; fiction novels, if two have an irreconcilable contradiction,&quot; if there's a need for levels of canon.<br /> <br /> You can still have wildly different &quot;settings&quot; in the same canon. WoD: Mirrors is canon. Or to go beyond TT RPGs, every Gundam TV show is canon despite most of them not sharing anything beyond big mechas some of which are called gundams.<br /> <br /> Canon is like a trademark without legal backing: a stamp of approval that the authority figure in question gives to a work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:10:14-07:00","id":1483526,"title":"","content":"Also, just to jump onto the other end of the question lest it go ignored:<br /> <br /> There's a lot of ChroD posts about mechanics because there's a lot of mechanics. These are not rules-lite games \u2014 in terms of sheer number of individual stats the average character sheet rivals if not surpasses what you'd find in DnD, and the franchise has historically done a lot of optional systems even before the formal shift to the Revised Storytelling System brought Chases and Investigations into the mix alongside the likes of combat and Social Maneuvering, to the point where two of my main hopes for the next edition are unified organization rules and a baseline system for ritual magic that isn't splat-specific.<br /> <br /> And talking of splat-specific magic, 2e in particular has taken pains to break up the 1e formula of &quot;every splat's powers work to some degree like Discipline effect ladders&quot; and &quot;every splat's non-fuel gauge runs on the same mechanics as Morality,&quot; while also introducing splats for which there is an explicit lack of high-level social organization from which generalized history can be inferred compared to sets of localized examples of strangeness and society. The existing lines' Second Editions have changed things here and there, but there's only so much conversation that can be generated from &quot;mummies can experience their separate Descents out of order now&quot; or &quot;werewolves can have kids with other werewolves without creating a spiritual nemesis now&quot; or &quot;changeling entitlements are now personal identity-roles instead of social affiliations&quot; without discussing particular games through APs or creating new material a la STV products.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, &quot;What are some good Praxes for a Mastigos with this concept?&quot; and &quot;Is it a good idea to save Vitriol Experiences for Pilgrimage instead of spending it on Azoth and calcified Alembics?&quot; and &quot;How do I optimize Endowment R&amp;D?&quot; are topics that people can easily present different takes on. Lore is interesting to read about and put to use, but as a topic of forum discussion it tends to live in the context of its original unpacking and not move too far from there without people going out of their way to carry it around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}